  // Titan Monuments and XP Arenas (the original, version 1.8, wiki Announcements): monuments replaced the old shard
  // lands; both have fixed difficulties; a monument gives "a % drop of a random Shard", an XP Arena raises the XP titans
  // gain and drops no relics or rewards ("these arenas are no walk in the park"); once battled in, each is unavailable
  // for 24 hours unless the player spends gems. Ours: the sites, their levels (a row of "battles" below), the Castle
  // that opens them, the defenders' AI, the battlefields, the stone cost (a raid's), the shard chances by stars and
  // amounts, the arena XP (x3 a land battle's) and the gem prices. Shards are one currency here, so "random" is the
  // chance itself. A won monument also gives a land battle's victory points (the original's rule for almost every win).
  "sites": {
    "cooldownHours": 24,
    "stones": 3,
    "shardPct": [40, 60, 80],
    "list": [
      { "id": "monument_bronze", "kind": "monument", "name": "Монумент Бронзы",  "level": 3, "castle": 5,  "shards": 1, "map": "map.ruins_01",    "resetGems": 30 },
