  // campaign "an economic way to rack up XP without spending a lot of portal stones". The wiki does not describe the
  // missions, so the story, acts, missions and star chests follow the master prompt (2.5 and 10.1-10.2): acts of 12
  // missions and a boss in its regions, Ilsa Wren's briefings, first-clear gems, star chests at 12/24/36 of 39 stars.
  // Ours: the enemy armies, levels, maps, the stone cost, the rewards and the Castle for each act. A mission's "level" is
  // the land battle row for its titan XP; the clients build its army from squads/tier/ai/titan. Missions go in order;
  // repeats give titan XP only. Types: field, hunt (a titan with a light escort), elite, boss.
